{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"30e8e41e5ab44c4e1c92faebc0aa2a6ead56ffc0a63dbf3043d95b85ca2a94ea","digest":{"component_or_area":"CI workflows (module-size gate)","key_entities":[".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml",".github/workflows/test.yml",".github/module-size-allowlist.txt","tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py","listed=$(grep -vE '^[[:space:]]*(#|$)' \"$allowlist\" | awk '{print $1}' | sort -u)"],"problem_keywords":["module-size gate","allowlist","empty allowlist","grep exit code","bash pipefail","CI shell robustness"],"propositions":["The module-size gate shell step fails with exit 1 when the allowlist is fully drained (contains only comments/empty lines) because grep returns exit 1 on no match, which aborts the step under bash -e -o pipefail before the over-cap check runs.","The fix wraps the grep command with '|| true' to tolerate the no-match exit code and allow the step to complete even when the allowlist is empty.","The identical listed= line must be guarded in both .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml and .github/workflows/test.yml to prevent the gate from breaking when the allowlist-draining change lands.","The gate must still fail (exit 1) when a file exceeds 800 LOC and is not in the allowlist, preserving the enforcement behavior for non-empty allowlists."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787463910760180001,"uuid":"62a51c2d-53f6-4e51-afbc-854f764c4115"}